  "id": "COMPOUND:23507 - PROTEIN:83",
  "verbalization": "K-strophanthin-beta is implicated in the activation of multiple targets, including the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1, T47D, and sodium/bile acid cotransporter, all of which ultimately lead to the glucagon receptor. This suggests a complex network of interactions where K-strophanthin-beta may influence downstream pathways that converge on the glucagon receptor. The evidence indicates that K-strophanthin-beta does not directly act on the glucagon receptor but rather through indirect mechanisms that involve other molecules. The high scores in the paths suggest a strong, though indirect, relationship, possibly mediated by intermediate targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of K-strophanthin-beta in modulating signaling networks that ultimately affect the glucagon receptor, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
